<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Arab%20Emirates.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Arab Emirates</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Gulf Cooperation Council is founded in Abu Dhabi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/malaysia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malaysia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malaysia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mahathir Mohamad becomes prime minister, serving until 2003</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kilwa-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kilwa%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kilwa Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The ruins of Kilwa Kisiwani and Songo Mnara become a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hellenic-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hellenic%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hellenic Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Greece becomes the tenth member of the European Communities; Andreas Papandreou's PASOK comes to power.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sadat is assassinated by an Islamic extremist; Hosni Mubarak succeeds him in a referendum in which he is the sole candidate.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Changi Airport opens, replacing Paya Lebar, as the Port of Singapore grows into one of the world's busiest and the economy turns to high-technology industry.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/solidarity"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Solidarity.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Solidarity</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Solidarity’s first national congress elects Wałęsa its president; in December martial law is imposed and the union’s leaders are jailed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/maoism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Maoism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Maoism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The party’s resolution on its history holds Mao chiefly responsible for the Cultural Revolution while upholding his Thought</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Congress follows Reagan’s proposal and cuts United States federal income taxes across the board by 25%</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzania commits to a National Economic Survival Programme of policy changes to liberalise its economy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/candomble"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Candombl%C3%A9.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Candomblé</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Brazilians take part in the first International Congress of Orisha Tradition and Culture in Ifẹ, Nigeria</span></li></ul></section>
